  "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
  "instance_name": "anchor_baby_rhetoric",
  "label": "Anchor Baby Rhetoric",
  "description": "This is a political and social trope that refers to the idea that children born to immigrants in a country (often the U.S.) are 'anchor babies' — meaning they are seen as a way for parents to gain legal residency or citizenship, and sometimes as a burden on the host country. The meme uses the image of a newborn baby to imply that the baby narrowly escaped harm because 'the democrats' didn't kill it — which is a direct reference to the 'anchor baby' rhetoric, which is often used to criticize immigration policies and to suggest that immigrants are taking advantage of the system. This trope is frequently used in anti-immigrant and anti-Democratic rhetoric.",
